<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="robots" content="noindex,nofollow"><title>Chinese 3 · Paper A · Answer guide</title><base href="/api/v1/course-tests/chinese-3/a/file/"><link rel="stylesheet" href="paper.css"></head><body><main><header class="hero"><p class="eyebrow">HSKKit · Chinese 3 Course Review · Original Paper A</p><h1>Answer guide</h1><p>40 objective questions + 4 writing/speaking tasks · 90-minute section budget.</p><p class="note">Reference materials. Open the workspace for section clocks, local answer saving and recording. Writing and speaking need self-review or your own teacher; no automatic grade.</p><nav class="links"><a href="index.html">Overview</a><a href="student.html">Learner paper</a><a href="student-traditional.html">繁體試卷</a><a href="teacher.html">Answers &amp; scripts</a><a href="listening.html">Listen to Chinese 3 A</a><a href="student.pdf">Learner PDF</a><a href="student-traditional.pdf">繁體 PDF</a><a href="teacher.pdf">Answer PDF</a></nav></header><nav class="links"><a href="#listening">Listening</a><a href="#reading">Reading</a><a href="#writing">Writing</a><a href="#speaking">Speaking</a></nav><h2 class="section-title" id="listening">Listening · 25 minutes</h2><h3>L1 · Questions 1–5</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/listening-group-1.mp3"></audio><p class="note">6:15 group track: 1 + 2 + 2 questions across three sources; each source plays twice, with answering pauses.</p><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-L1a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 1</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">female · 那是上学期刚开学的时候。我第一次去学校的志愿活动，负责带新同学找教室。出发前我把路线走了两遍，没想到活动结束后，我自己也认识了几个朋友。我本来以为自己还不熟悉校园，不能帮上忙。</p></div><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/c3a-l1a.mp3"></audio><p class="gloss">志愿活动: volunteer activity</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q1"><h3>1. When did the speaker first help at this school activity?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 上学期刚开学时</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 上学期结束时</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 这学期放假以后</div></div><div class="key"><b>Answer: A</b><p>She locates the first visit at the beginning of last term.</p><p class="cn">她把这次初次参加的经历定位在上学期刚开学时。</p><b>Evidence</b><p class="cn">那是上学期刚开学的时候</p><ul><li>B: The end of the activity is not the end of the school term.<br>活动结束不等于学期结束，材料没有说学期末。</li><li>C: Neither this term nor a holiday is given as the time.<br>材料没有把时间放在本学期放假后。</li></ul></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-L1b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 2, 3 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">male · 第一次介绍社团时，我准备了一大段话，以为新同学会站着听完。可是他们经过桌子时，只问能不能亲手试一试，很少有人看我的介绍板。</p><p class="cn">female · 后来你怎么改的？</p><p class="cn">male · 第二次我先拿出材料，让大家做一个小东西，再回答他们的问题。虽然我说的话少了，留下来参加的人却多了。我才发现，他们想先知道自己能做什么。有几个原来走开的同学，也回来问下次什么时候还能参加。</p></div><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/c3a-l1b.mp3"></audio><p class="gloss">介绍板: display board</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q2"><h3>2. What had the man expected before his first introduction?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 新同学会先动手做东西</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 新同学都会带材料来</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 新同学会听完长介绍</div></div><div class="key"><b>Answer: C</b><p>He expected newcomers to listen to his prepared talk.</p><p class="cn">他原先以为新同学会站着听完准备的长介绍。</p><b>Evidence</b><p class="cn">以为新同学会站着听完</p><ul><li>A: Hands-on activity was the later change, not the original expectation.<br>先动手是后来调整的办法，不是原先期待。</li><li>B: He does not expect newcomers to bring supplies.<br>材料没有说他以为新同学会自带材料。</li></ul></div></article><article class="question" id="q3"><h3>3. Why did the second introduction attract more participants?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 把原来的介绍讲得更长</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 不再回答新同学的问题</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 先让大家体验自己能做什么</div></div><div class="key"><b>Answer: C</b><p>The change matches the visitors’ expressed wish to try an activity before hearing details.</p><p class="cn">前一次大家想亲手尝试，后来先让他们体验再回答问题，回应了这项需要。</p><b>Evidence</b><p class="cn">只问能不能亲手试一试</p><p class="cn">让大家做一个小东西，再回答他们的问题</p><ul><li>A: The man explicitly says he talked less the second time.<br>他说第二次说的话少了，不是介绍更长了。</li><li>B: He still answered questions after the activity.<br>他仍然回答问题，只是改在体验之后。</li></ul></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-L1c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 4, 5 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">female · 我们的小组消息太多了。我想认真参加，可是晚上九点以后不想再看群消息，还要留时间读书。</p><p class="cn">male · 我也常常一边做作业一边等回复。我们可以每天八点统一发一次分工，临时想到的小问题先记下来，第二天再讨论。</p><p class="cn">female · 这样我九点就能放心把手机放下了。急事还是可以打电话。</p><p class="cn">male · 好，我把这个办法告诉大家。要更改的地方，可以在那条消息下面写，不用每次都另发。不是让谁退出小组。</p></div><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/c3a-l1c.mp3"></audio><p class="gloss">群消息: group-chat messages</p><p class="gloss">分工: division of tasks</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q4"><h3>4. What need does the woman state?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 每天八点以前完成所有作业</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 完全不参加小组讨论</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 九点以后不再看群消息</div></div><div class="key"><b>Answer: C</b><p>She wants a clear nine-o’clock boundary for group messages.</p><p class="cn">她明确提出九点以后不再看群消息。</p><b>Evidence</b><p class="cn">晚上九点以后不想再看群消息</p><ul><li>A: Eight o’clock is the suggested message time, not a homework deadline.<br>八点是统一发消息的建议时间，不是作业截止时间。</li><li>B: She says she wants to participate seriously.<br>她说想认真参加，并非不讨论。</li></ul></div></article><article class="question" id="q5"><h3>5. What is the likely purpose of the man’s proposal?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 让大家以后只用电话交流</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 减少一直等消息的负担，同时保留合作</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 让不及时回复的人退出小组</div></div><div class="key"><b>Answer: B</b><p>A fixed update time addresses constant waiting while preserving shared work.</p><p class="cn">固定更新时间能减少一直等待，又能继续分工合作；这是对两处线索的有限推断。</p><b>Evidence</b><p class="cn">一边做作业一边等回复</p><p class="cn">每天八点统一发一次分工，临时想到的小问题先记下来，第二天再讨论</p><ul><li>A: Calls are kept for urgent matters, not made the only method.<br>电话只保留给急事，没有变成唯一方式。</li><li>C: He explicitly says the idea is not to make someone leave.<br>他明确说不是让谁退出。</li></ul></div></article></div></section><h3>L2 · Questions 6–10</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/listening-group-2.mp3"></audio><p class="note">6:15 group track: 1 + 2 + 2 questions across three sources; each source plays twice, with answering pauses.</p><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-L2a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 6</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">male · 我想下学期参加学校的讲故事活动。现在我说话容易忘记顺序，所以这个月先每周借一本短故事，读完以后用自己的话讲给弟弟听。这样不用一次讲得很长，也能练习把经过连起来。报名的事，等我练习一段时间再决定。</p></div><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/c3a-l2a.mp3"></audio><p class="gloss">报名: sign up</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q6"><h3>6. What will the speaker do first to prepare for the future activity?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 这个月马上报名参加</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 请弟弟替自己讲故事</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 每周读故事并试着复述</div></div><div class="key"><b>Answer: C</b><p>He names weekly reading and retelling as the immediate preparation.</p><p class="cn">他明确先每周读一本短故事，再用自己的话讲给弟弟听。</p><b>Evidence</b><p class="cn">这个月先每周借一本短故事，读完以后用自己的话讲给弟弟听</p><ul><li>A: He postpones deciding about registration until after practice.<br>报名要等练习一段时间以后再决定。</li><li>B: The speaker will tell the story; his brother is the listener.<br>讲故事的是说话者，弟弟是听众。</li></ul></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-L2b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 7, 8 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">female · 学校有两个体验活动。甲是周六上午的校园广播课，参加的人星期五前要交一段自己写的介绍。乙是周日下午的摄影课，要自己带相机。</p><p class="cn">male · 我只在周六上午有空，也想练习把事情说清楚。相机我没有，不过我已经写过一篇社团介绍，还可以请老师帮我修改。</p><p class="cn">female · 那你先把介绍改好，看看报名说明，再确认甲活动还有没有位置。符合时间不代表已经报上名了。</p></div><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/c3a-l2b.mp3"></audio><p class="gloss">校园广播: school radio</p><p class="gloss">摄影: photography</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q7"><h3>7. What preparation is required for Activity A?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 星期五前交自己写的介绍</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 周日下午自己带相机</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 先买一台新的相机</div></div><div class="key"><b>Answer: A</b><p>Activity A requires a self-written introduction before Friday.</p><p class="cn">甲活动要求星期五前交一段自己写的介绍。</p><b>Evidence</b><p class="cn">参加的人星期五前要交一段自己写的介绍</p><ul><li>B: Sunday and a camera belong to Activity B.<br>周日带相机是乙活动的要求。</li><li>C: Buying a new camera is not a requirement of either stated plan.<br>两个所述方案都没有要求先买新相机。</li></ul></div></article><article class="question" id="q8"><h3>8. Which next step fits the man’s situation?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 直接认定自己已报上甲活动</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 改去只在周日下午开的乙活动</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 修改介绍后确认甲活动是否有名额</div></div><div class="key"><b>Answer: C</b><p>A fits his time and speaking goal, but he still needs to prepare and check availability.</p><p class="cn">甲符合时间和表达目标，但还须改好介绍并确认名额。</p><b>Evidence</b><p class="cn">我只在周六上午有空，也想练习把事情说清楚</p><p class="cn">先把介绍改好，看看报名说明，再确认甲活动还有没有位置</p><ul><li>A: The woman distinguishes being available from being registered.<br>女生明确区分时间合适与已经报名。</li><li>B: He says he is available only on Saturday morning.<br>他明确只在周六上午有空。</li></ul></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-L2c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 9, 10 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">female · 苏安负责找资料，陈林负责录音，我来把两部分放在一起。原来想星期三晚上全部做完，可陈林那天有球赛。</p><p class="cn">male · 录音最好用完整的资料，不能先随便录一段。苏安星期二放学后能发来资料吗？</p><p class="cn">female · 可以。陈林说星期四晚上能录好，我星期五午休时整理。</p><p class="cn">male · 那就按这个顺序来。我们星期五下午交，只要每个人在前一步之后完成自己的部分，就来得及。</p></div><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/c3a-l2c.mp3"></audio><p class="gloss">录音: record audio</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q9"><h3>9. Who is responsible for finding the information?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 陈林</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 苏安</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 最后整理的人</div></div><div class="key"><b>Answer: B</b><p>The first speaker assigns information gathering to Su’an.</p><p class="cn">开头明确由苏安找资料。</p><b>Evidence</b><p class="cn">苏安负责找资料，陈林负责录音</p><ul><li>A: Chen Lin is assigned recording.<br>陈林负责录音。</li><li>C: The woman puts the parts together, rather than being named as the researcher.<br>女生负责把两部分放在一起，没有被指定找资料。</li></ul></div></article><article class="question" id="q10"><h3>10. What sequence have they finally agreed on?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 周二资料，周四录音，周五整理后交</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 周三先录音，再等周四的资料</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 周五交完以后再整理</div></div><div class="key"><b>Answer: A</b><p>Combining the confirmed dates gives information first, recording next, then assembly before submission.</p><p class="cn">把两处确认的日期合起来，可知先资料、再录音、最后整理后提交。</p><b>Evidence</b><p class="cn">苏安星期二放学后能发来资料吗</p><p class="cn">陈林说星期四晚上能录好，我星期五午休时整理</p><ul><li>B: They reject recording without complete information, and the recording is moved to Thursday.<br>他们反对资料不全就录音，录音时间也已改到周四。</li><li>C: Assembly at Friday lunch precedes Friday afternoon submission.<br>周五午休整理在下午提交之前。</li></ul></div></article></div></section><h3>L3 · Questions 11–15</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/listening-group-3.mp3"></audio><p class="note">6:15 group track: 1 + 2 + 2 questions across three sources; each source plays twice, with answering pauses.</p><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-L3a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 11</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">female · 本周的校园节目不教大家怎样比赛，也不公布社团名单。我们采访了两位同学，请他们说说一次失败以后怎样改变做法。每一段都保留了最初的困难和后来的选择。听完他们的经历，你也可以想想自己学会了什么。</p></div><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/c3a-l3a.mp3"></audio><p class="gloss">采访: interview</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q11"><h3>11. What is the main purpose of this programme?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 公布下一次比赛的获奖名单</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 介绍同学从经历中改变做法的故事</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 教授参加比赛必须使用的方法</div></div><div class="key"><b>Answer: B</b><p>It introduces interviews about learning from an experience and changing an approach.</p><p class="cn">节目介绍同学如何从一次经历中改变做法。</p><b>Evidence</b><p class="cn">请他们说说一次失败以后怎样改变做法</p><ul><li>A: No winners are announced.<br>没有公布获奖名单。</li><li>C: It explicitly says it does not teach how to compete.<br>开头明确说不教大家怎样比赛。</li></ul></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-L3b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 12, 13 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">male · 故事里的小雨一直想买一本漂亮的新本子，觉得旧本子没有用了。整理时，她发现旧本子上有爷爷教她画的第一棵树，还有自己写错以后改过的字。她决定买一本新本子上课，把旧本子留下来画画。</p><p class="cn">female · 她最后认为所有旧东西都不能扔吗？</p><p class="cn">male · 没有。结尾只写，她不再只看封面新不新，而会先看看里面记着什么。她还把已经用不上的空盒子送给了需要的同学。</p></div><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/c3a-l3b.mp3"></audio><p class="gloss">封面: cover</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q12"><h3>12. How does Xiaoyu’s view of the notebook change?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 从只看新旧，变为注意里面记录的经历</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 从想买新本子，变为以后都不用新本子</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 从喜欢画画，变为只愿意写字</div></div><div class="key"><b>Answer: A</b><p>The old drawings and corrections lead her to value the recorded experience, while still buying a notebook for class.</p><p class="cn">旧画和改字让她注意记录的经历；她仍买新本子上课，观点不是绝对反对新本子。</p><b>Evidence</b><p class="cn">觉得旧本子没有用了</p><p class="cn">把旧本子留下来画画</p><p class="cn">会先看看里面记着什么</p><ul><li>B: She still decides to buy a new notebook for class.<br>她仍决定买一本新本子上课。</li><li>C: She keeps the old notebook specifically for drawing.<br>她留下旧本子正是为了画画。</li></ul></div></article><article class="question" id="q13"><h3>13. Which attitude is best supported by the ending?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 按具体用途和记忆决定去留</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 旧东西越多就一定越好</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 只要封面漂亮就应该留下</div></div><div class="key"><b>Answer: A</b><p>Keeping meaningful records but giving away unneeded boxes supports a case-by-case decision.</p><p class="cn">既留有意义的记录，又送出不用的盒子，支持按具体情况决定，而非一概保留。</p><b>Evidence</b><p class="cn">会先看看里面记着什么</p><p class="cn">把已经用不上的空盒子送给了需要的同学</p><ul><li>B: The ending includes giving away unneeded objects.<br>结尾包含送出不用的物品，并非越多越好。</li><li>C: She moves away from judging only by the cover.<br>她已经不再只看封面。</li></ul></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-L3c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 14, 15 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">female · 周六学校有重复使用活动。上午十点到十二点修补布袋，来之前要把要修的袋子洗干净，工具可以向老师借。下午两点到四点整理旧书，两项都不用交钱。</p><p class="cn">male · 我只有上午有空，家里正好有一个提手破了的布袋。我想学着把它修好，以后继续用。</p><p class="cn">female · 那就提前准备好袋子。老师会带着大家做，具体从哪一步开始，可以先问现场的老师。别把下午整理旧书的时间记成上午。</p></div><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/c3a-l3c.mp3"></audio><p class="gloss">修补: mend</p><p class="gloss">提手: handle</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q14"><h3>14. What must participants do before the morning activity?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 先交修补工具的钱</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 把要修的布袋洗干净</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 先把所有旧书整理完</div></div><div class="key"><b>Answer: B</b><p>The preparation requirement is to wash the bag.</p><p class="cn">明确要求来之前把要修的布袋洗干净。</p><b>Evidence</b><p class="cn">来之前要把要修的袋子洗干净</p><ul><li>A: Tools can be borrowed and both activities are free.<br>工具可借，两项也都免费。</li><li>C: Book sorting is the separate afternoon activity.<br>整理旧书是下午的另一项活动。</li></ul></div></article><article class="question" id="q15"><h3>15. Which plan fits the man’s availability and goal?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 下午参加旧书整理</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 下午才开始修补布袋</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 上午参加布袋修补</div></div><div class="key"><b>Answer: C</b><p>Morning mending matches both his available time and his wish to reuse the bag.</p><p class="cn">上午修袋既符合空闲时间，也符合继续使用破袋子的目标。</p><b>Evidence</b><p class="cn">我只有上午有空</p><p class="cn">我想学着把它修好，以后继续用</p><ul><li>A: He is not available in the afternoon, and book sorting does not meet his stated goal.<br>他下午没空，整理旧书也不对应修袋目标。</li><li>B: Bag mending is scheduled in the morning.<br>修补布袋安排在上午，不在下午。</li></ul></div></article></div></section><h3>L4 · Questions 16–20</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/listening-group-4.mp3"></audio><p class="note">6:15 group track: 1 + 2 + 2 questions across three sources; each source plays twice, with answering pauses.</p><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-L4a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 16</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">male · 原定周五下午收集可重复使用的纸盒，现在改到周六上午九点。因为周五要先检查教室，不能提前堆放东西。收集地点还是教学楼门口，只改日期和时间。如果已经和同学约好，请记得把新时间告诉对方。</p></div><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/c3a-l4a.mp3"></audio><p class="gloss">堆放: pile up</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q16"><h3>16. What is the revised collection time?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 周六上午九点</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 周五下午九点</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 周六下午原定时间</div></div><div class="key"><b>Answer: A</b><p>The update explicitly moves collection to Saturday at nine in the morning.</p><p class="cn">通知明确改为周六上午九点。</p><b>Evidence</b><p class="cn">现在改到周六上午九点</p><ul><li>B: Friday is the old date and nine is a morning time.<br>周五是旧日期，九点也明确为上午。</li><li>C: The recording specifies Saturday morning, not afternoon.<br>录音明确是周六上午，不是下午。</li></ul></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-L4b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 17, 18 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">female · 小宁以前写完作业就一直看手机，第二天常觉得准备东西很匆忙。这个月她试着睡前半小时不用手机，先把书包放好，再读一小段书。她不是每天都做得到，不过大多数晚上能按计划结束。</p><p class="cn">male · 她觉得有什么不同？</p><p class="cn">female · 两周后她说，早上少了到处找东西的着急，出门也从容一些。她觉得这个安排比较容易重复做。她没有说这办法适合所有人，只打算再试一段时间。</p></div><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/c3a-l4b.mp3"></audio><p class="gloss">匆忙: hurried</p><p class="gloss">从容: unhurried</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q17"><h3>17. What change does Xiaoning try this month?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 一写完作业就立刻出门</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 睡前半小时不用手机</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 每天早上多花半小时找东西</div></div><div class="key"><b>Answer: B</b><p>This is the explicitly stated habit change.</p><p class="cn">这是材料明确给出的习惯改变。</p><b>Evidence</b><p class="cn">睡前半小时不用手机</p><ul><li>A: Going out immediately after homework is not described.<br>材料没有说写完作业就出门。</li><li>C: She reports less morning searching, not adding time for it.<br>她报告早上少了找东西的着急，不是增加找东西时间。</li></ul></div></article><article class="question" id="q18"><h3>18. What explains her reported change in the morning?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 两周以后不再需要准备书包</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 晚上先放好书包，早上少了找东西</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 她保证每天都完全做到计划</div></div><div class="key"><b>Answer: B</b><p>Preparing the bag in the evening matches her report of less searching in the morning.</p><p class="cn">晚上先准备书包，与早上减少寻找的报告相对应；只解释材料中的个人经历。</p><b>Evidence</b><p class="cn">先把书包放好</p><p class="cn">早上少了到处找东西的着急</p><ul><li>A: Preparing the bag is still part of the routine.<br>准备书包仍是习惯的一部分。</li><li>C: The source explicitly says she does not manage it every day.<br>原文说不是每天都做得到，不能变成每天保证。</li></ul></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-L4c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 19, 20 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">male · 去年我为了参加长跑活动，放学后常和朋友一起在操场走一会儿。那次没有得到奖，可我记得最清楚的是大家边走边聊天，心情比一个人闷着好。</p><p class="cn">female · 我最近也想活动一下，可每天只能空出十分钟，没时间准备比赛。</p><p class="cn">male · 那先约朋友走十分钟吧，不必把目标定成比赛。如果那天太忙，也可以改到第二天，不必一次做得很久。我原来只想着名次，后来才发现，愿意一起坚持的人也很重要。</p></div><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/c3a-l4c.mp3"></audio><p class="gloss">长跑: distance running</p><p class="gloss">闷着: keep feelings to oneself</p><p class="gloss">名次: placing in a competition</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q19"><h3>19. Which suggestion fits the woman’s present circumstances?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 每天练习一小时再决定是否活动</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 约朋友走十分钟，不以比赛为目标</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 等到有完整比赛时间才开始活动</div></div><div class="key"><b>Answer: B</b><p>A short walk uses her available time and does not require preparing for a competition.</p><p class="cn">短时间同行符合十分钟空闲，也不要求准备比赛。</p><b>Evidence</b><p class="cn">每天只能空出十分钟，没时间准备比赛</p><p class="cn">那先约朋友走十分钟吧，不必把目标定成比赛</p><ul><li>A: An hour exceeds her stated available time.<br>一小时超过她所说的空闲时间。</li><li>C: The man explicitly separates being active from competing.<br>男生明确把活动与比赛分开，不必等有比赛时间。</li></ul></div></article><article class="question" id="q20"><h3>20. What does the man’s reflection suggest he now values?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 共同坚持的过程，不只看名次</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 只有得到奖才算值得参加</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 不再愿意和朋友一起活动</div></div><div class="key"><b>Answer: A</b><p>His memory and reflection support valuing shared persistence as well as results.</p><p class="cn">未获奖仍记得同行过程，并说一起坚持的人重要，支持不只重名次的反思。</p><b>Evidence</b><p class="cn">那次没有得到奖</p><p class="cn">愿意一起坚持的人也很重要</p><ul><li>B: He recalls value despite receiving no award.<br>没有获奖仍有值得记住的内容，不支持唯奖论。</li><li>C: His recommendation is to walk with friends.<br>他的建议正是约朋友同行。</li></ul></div></article></div></section><h2 class="section-title" id="reading">Reading · 30 minutes</h2><h3>R1 · Questions 21–25</h3><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-R1a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 21</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">上学期第一个星期五，学校请我们帮助新同学。我原来以为自己要站在门口讲话，到了才知道，老师让我陪两位同学找实验教室。我先看了楼层图，再带他们上楼。那天下午我说的话不多，却一直在认真听他们的问题。回家后，我把这次第一次帮助别人的经历写进了日记。</p></div><p class="gloss">实验教室: science classroom</p><p class="gloss">楼层图: floor plan</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q21"><h3>21. When did the writer help the new students?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 上学期最后一个星期五</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 上学期第一个星期五</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 本学期第一天</div></div><div class="key"><b>Answer: B</b><p>The first sentence supplies the specific day.</p><p class="cn">第一句明确给出上学期第一个星期五。</p><b>Evidence</b><p class="cn">上学期第一个星期五</p><ul><li>A: The text says first, not last.<br>原文是第一个，不是最后一个。</li><li>C: The text refers to last term, not this term’s first day.<br>原文指上学期，不是本学期第一天。</li></ul></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-R1b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 22, 23 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">我参加校刊小组以前，总以为采访就是提前写好问题，再请对方一个个回答。第一次采访门口的保安叔叔时，我把问题问完就准备离开。他笑着问，我要不要听听他最难忘的一天。我这才放下本子，认真听他讲有一次怎样帮助迷路的新生。<br>回到小组，我没有按原来的问题顺序写文章，而是先写那一天发生的事，再补上人物介绍。老师说，读者因此更容易了解他的工作。我发现，准备问题当然有用，但愿意听对方想讲的事情也很重要。下次采访，我还会准备问题，却不会只盯着自己的本子。</p></div><p class="gloss">校刊: school magazine</p><p class="gloss">保安: security guard</p><p class="gloss">新生: new student</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q22"><h3>22. What did the writer originally expect an interview to be?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 完全不用提前准备任何问题</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 由被采访的人替自己写文章</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 按事先写好的问题逐个问答</div></div><div class="key"><b>Answer: C</b><p>The original idea is a prepared question-by-question exchange.</p><p class="cn">原先以为采访就是按准备的问题逐个问答。</p><b>Evidence</b><p class="cn">总以为采访就是提前写好问题，再请对方一个个回答</p><ul><li>A: The writer explicitly prepared questions.<br>作者明确有提前准备问题。</li><li>B: The interviewee is not expected to write the article.<br>材料没有说由被采访者写文章。</li></ul></div></article><article class="question" id="q23"><h3>23. Why did the writer change the article’s organization?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 因为老师要求删除所有人物介绍</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 因为原来没有准备任何采访问题</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 先呈现具体经历，更便于读者理解人物工作</div></div><div class="key"><b>Answer: C</b><p>The new order places the concrete event before background, which the teacher links to reader understanding.</p><p class="cn">先事件再人物介绍的组织，与更容易理解工作相联系。</p><b>Evidence</b><p class="cn">先写那一天发生的事，再补上人物介绍</p><p class="cn">读者因此更容易了解他的工作</p><ul><li>A: The background introduction is added later, not deleted.<br>人物介绍是随后补上，不是全部删除。</li><li>B: The passage explicitly says the questions had been prepared.<br>材料明确说明事先准备了问题。</li></ul></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-R1c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 24, 25 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">小组通知：我们要在周四放学前交一份校园生活介绍。周二请每个人提出一个主题，周三中午一起确定内容。资料可以从校园观察中获得，不要求采访校外的人。每个人都要负责一小部分，不能只由一位同学完成。<br>小梅回复：我周三中午要参加合唱练习，不能开会。我愿意整理食堂排队的观察，周二晚上就把笔记发给大家。请你们先讨论；如果主题合适，再告诉我需要补什么。我周四午休还能修改，但放学后不能留下来。</p></div><p class="gloss">合唱: choir</p><p class="gloss">排队: queue</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q24"><h3>24. By when must the group submit its introduction?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 周三中午开会前</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 周四放学前</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 周四放学以后</div></div><div class="key"><b>Answer: B</b><p>The notice sets submission before school finishes on Thursday.</p><p class="cn">通知规定周四放学前交。</p><b>Evidence</b><p class="cn">周四放学前交一份校园生活介绍</p><ul><li>A: Wednesday lunch is the discussion time, not the final deadline.<br>周三中午是讨论时间，不是最终截止。</li><li>C: After school would miss the stated deadline.<br>放学后才交会错过明确期限。</li></ul></div></article><article class="question" id="q25"><h3>25. What is a reasonable next action for the other members?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 等周四放学后再让她开始找资料</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 周三讨论她的笔记，尽早反馈供她周四午休修改</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 因为她不能开会，就认定她不能参与</div></div><div class="key"><b>Answer: B</b><p>The notice’s meeting time and her available revision time support discussing the notes and giving timely feedback.</p><p class="cn">把讨论时间和她能修改的时间结合，可推断应及时反馈，而非等待放学后。</p><b>Evidence</b><p class="cn">周三中午一起确定内容</p><p class="cn">我周四午休还能修改，但放学后不能留下来</p><ul><li>A: The proposed delay conflicts with both the deadline and her availability.<br>等放学后既与截止时间冲突，也与她的空闲冲突。</li><li>C: She offers notes and revision, so missing one meeting does not imply no contribution.<br>她主动提供笔记并愿意修改，缺席一次会议不等于不能参与。</li></ul></div></article></div></section><h3>R2 · Questions 26–30</h3><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-R2a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 26</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">林安想在下学期参加学校的故事分享小组。她喜欢读书，却发现自己讲故事时容易漏掉中间的经过。她给这个月定了一个小目标：每周读完一篇短故事，写下三个先后发生的动作，再试着不看书讲给同伴听。她暂时没有报名，准备月末听听同伴的意见，再决定是否参加。</p></div><p class="gloss">漏掉: leave out</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q26"><h3>26. What is Lin’an’s preparation plan for this month?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 每周读故事，记动作顺序，再试着复述</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 先报名，再请别人代替自己读书</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 只记故事结尾，不再练习讲述</div></div><div class="key"><b>Answer: A</b><p>The plan combines reading, sequencing and retelling.</p><p class="cn">计划包括读、记录动作顺序以及尝试复述。</p><b>Evidence</b><p class="cn">每周读完一篇短故事，写下三个先后发生的动作，再试着不看书讲给同伴听</p><ul><li>B: She has not registered and does not plan to delegate reading.<br>她暂未报名，也没有请别人替自己读。</li><li>C: She records three actions, not only an ending.<br>她记录三个动作，并非只记结尾。</li></ul></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-R2b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 27, 28 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">下月学校开放两种体验活动。甲是星期六上午的讲解练习，参加者先观察一处校园空间，再在周五前交一份简短介绍。老师提供图片，不需要自己买设备。乙是星期日下午的影像记录，参加者须带能够拍摄的设备，并提前学习一种剪辑工具。两个活动都可以帮助同学整理信息，但练习方式不同。<br>小禾希望以后能把复杂事情讲得更清楚。她只有星期六上午有空，已经记下了图书角的使用情况，却还没有整理成介绍。她不想为了这次活动购买设备。她准备先看清要求，再确认是否还有位置，不会仅因时间合适就当作报名成功。</p></div><p class="gloss">剪辑: video editing</p><p class="gloss">设备: equipment</p><p class="gloss">图书角: classroom reading corner</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q27"><h3>27. Which difference between the activities is stated?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 甲练习讲解并提供图片，乙要带拍摄设备</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 甲要求购买设备，乙完全不需要准备</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 甲乙都只在星期日下午进行</div></div><div class="key"><b>Answer: A</b><p>Activity A focuses on explanation with supplied pictures, while B requires filming equipment.</p><p class="cn">甲提供图片并练习讲解，乙要求自带拍摄设备；两者的准备和表达方式不同。</p><b>Evidence</b><p class="cn">老师提供图片，不需要自己买设备</p><p class="cn">参加者须带能够拍摄的设备</p><ul><li>B: A is said not to require equipment purchases, and B has preparation requirements.<br>甲不要求买设备，乙也不是完全不需准备。</li><li>C: A is on Saturday morning; B is on Sunday afternoon.<br>甲在周六上午，乙在周日下午。</li></ul></div></article><article class="question" id="q28"><h3>28. Which action best matches Xiaohe’s goal and constraints?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 购买新设备后报名乙，不考虑周日时间</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 把观察整理成介绍，再询问甲的名额</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 仅凭甲的时间合适就停止准备</div></div><div class="key"><b>Answer: B</b><p>A fits her goal and time, but she must turn her notes into the required introduction and confirm a place.</p><p class="cn">甲符合表达目标和时间，但仍须整理介绍并确认名额。</p><b>Evidence</b><p class="cn">希望以后能把复杂事情讲得更清楚</p><p class="cn">只有星期六上午有空</p><p class="cn">还没有整理成介绍</p><ul><li>A: Buying equipment does not resolve her lack of Sunday availability.<br>购买设备并不能解决周日没空的问题。</li><li>C: Her introduction is unfinished and she has not confirmed a place.<br>介绍尚未完成，也未确认名额，不能停止准备。</li></ul></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-R2c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 29, 30 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">活动公告：读书社本周要制作一张共同推荐单。每人选择一个校园生活话题，写出自己的看法和一个具体例子。周三晚上八点前发给负责人，周四中午讨论，再于放学前定稿。推荐单不要求所有人意见相同，但每一项都要说明理由。<br>周宁的回复：我想谈午休时怎样使用图书角。我认为应该留出安静读书的地方，因为上次大家同时讨论时，有同学没法专心。我周四中午有事，不过周三晚上七点能发来内容，也愿意在讨论前补充一个例子。请把讨论后的修改意见发给我，我当天放学前还有时间调整。</p></div><p class="gloss">推荐单: recommendation list</p><p class="gloss">定稿: finalize</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q29"><h3>29. What reason does Zhou Ning give for a quiet reading space?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 负责人要求所有人意见一样</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 图书角周四中午将不开放</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 讨论声曾影响同学专心读书</div></div><div class="key"><b>Answer: C</b><p>The reason is a past observation of discussion disturbing concentration.</p><p class="cn">理由来自过去讨论影响专心的观察。</p><b>Evidence</b><p class="cn">上次大家同时讨论时，有同学没法专心</p><ul><li>A: The notice explicitly allows different opinions.<br>公告明确不要求所有人意见相同。</li><li>B: No Thursday closure is announced.<br>材料没有说图书角周四关闭。</li></ul></div></article><article class="question" id="q30"><h3>30. Does Zhou Ning’s proposed contribution fit the stated process?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 可以，七点先交看法和例子，再按讨论意见修改</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 不可以，因为公告禁止缺席会议的人交内容</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 可以，但必须等周四讨论结束才第一次交内容</div></div><div class="key"><b>Answer: A</b><p>The proposed initial submission is before eight; later revision fits the discussion process.</p><p class="cn">七点初稿早于八点截止，之后又能按讨论意见调整，符合流程。</p><b>Evidence</b><p class="cn">周三晚上八点前发给负责人</p><p class="cn">周三晚上七点能发来内容</p><p class="cn">当天放学前还有时间调整</p><ul><li>B: The notice does not prohibit contributions from someone missing the meeting.<br>公告没有禁止缺席会议者贡献内容。</li><li>C: Waiting until after the discussion would miss the initial submission deadline.<br>首次提交若等到讨论后，会错过周三初稿截止。</li></ul></div></article></div></section><h3>R3 · Questions 31–35</h3><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-R3a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 31</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">校园广播本周开设“试过以后”小栏目，不介绍比赛成绩，而请同学讲一次自己改变办法的经历。第一期有人谈怎样从只读书名改成先翻目录，也有人谈怎样把难记的路线画出来。节目最后会请听众选择一种愿意尝试的办法，并写下一周后的感受。栏目并不保证每种办法都适合每个人。</p></div><p class="gloss">栏目: programme segment</p><p class="gloss">目录: table of contents</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q31"><h3>31. What is the main idea of this programme introduction?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 分享改变做法的经历，并鼓励有选择地尝试</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 按比赛成绩给全校同学排出名次</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 保证听众使用同一种办法都能成功</div></div><div class="key"><b>Answer: A</b><p>The segment shares experience-based changes and invites a selective trial.</p><p class="cn">栏目分享改变办法的经历，并请听众选择尝试。</p><b>Evidence</b><p class="cn">请同学讲一次自己改变办法的经历</p><ul><li>B: It explicitly does not introduce competition results.<br>开头明确不介绍比赛成绩。</li><li>C: It explicitly avoids promising that every method fits everyone.<br>末句明确不保证每种办法适合每个人。</li></ul></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-R3b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 32, 33 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">短故事《不一样的礼物》中，小岚想给朋友做一本相册。她起初只找颜色漂亮的纸，觉得好看就够了。后来她看到朋友保留的一张模糊照片：那是两人第一次一起完成小组任务时拍的。照片并不清楚，朋友却把它放在书桌上。<br>小岚于是把那张照片放在相册第一页，旁边写下当时大家怎样互相帮忙。其他页面仍然用了她喜欢的彩纸，但每页都多了一段小记。朋友说，自己最喜欢的是那些一起经历过的事。故事结尾，朋友把相册放在常看的书架上，翻到第一页，笑着又说起那天的事。小岚看着旁边还没用完的彩纸，决定留着做下一份礼物。</p></div><p class="gloss">相册: photo album</p><p class="gloss">模糊: blurred</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q32"><h3>32. Why does Xiaolan put the unclear photo on the first page?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 因为朋友只喜欢看不清楚的照片</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 它记录了两人共同完成任务的经历</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 因为她决定整本相册不再用彩纸</div></div><div class="key"><b>Answer: B</b><p>The photo’s shared event and her added account of mutual help explain the choice.</p><p class="cn">照片记录共同任务，旁边又写互相帮助，说明选择重在共同经历。</p><b>Evidence</b><p class="cn">两人第一次一起完成小组任务时拍的</p><p class="cn">旁边写下当时大家怎样互相帮忙</p><ul><li>A: The friend values this photo, but the text does not generalize a preference for unclear photos.<br>朋友珍惜这一张，不等于只喜欢模糊照片。</li><li>C: She continues to use coloured paper on other pages.<br>其他页面仍用了彩纸。</li></ul></div></article><article class="question" id="q33"><h3>33. Which interpretation best fits the ending?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 外观之外，共同经历也能让礼物有意义</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 所有好看的礼物都没有价值</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 只有模糊照片才值得保存</div></div><div class="key"><b>Answer: A</b><p>The ending adds the value of shared memories without denying appearance.</p><p class="cn">结尾增加共同记忆的意义，没有否定外观的价值。</p><b>Evidence</b><p class="cn">翻到第一页，笑着又说起那天的事</p><p class="cn">决定留着做下一份礼物</p><ul><li>B: Xiaolan keeps the coloured paper for another gift, so the ending does not dismiss appearance.<br>小岚还留着彩纸做下一份礼物，不支持否定外观价值。</li><li>C: The value comes from the experience, not the photo being unclear.<br>价值来自经历，不是模糊本身。</li></ul></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-R3c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 34, 35 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">学校准备举行一次旧物再用活动。修补区只接收已经清洗的布袋，工具由老师提供，参加者须先说明哪里需要修补。分享区接收内容完整、适合同龄人阅读的旧书，不收缺页的练习册。两个区域都在周六上午开放，大家可以按自己的需要选择，不必每个区域都去。<br>小齐想让破了一个小口的布袋继续使用，家里的几本书也想带来。她周六只有一个小时，因此决定先把袋子洗好，再检查书页。如果书适合分享，就在修袋前先送到分享区；如果书有缺页，就暂时留下处理，而不是把它交给别人。她最想完成的仍是修好布袋。</p></div><p class="gloss">缺页: missing pages</p><p class="gloss">同龄人: people of the same age</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q34"><h3>34. What does the sharing area refuse?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 缺页的练习册</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 内容完整且适合同龄人的旧书</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 所有已经读过的书</div></div><div class="key"><b>Answer: A</b><p>The stated exclusion is workbooks with missing pages.</p><p class="cn">明确不收的是缺页的练习册。</p><b>Evidence</b><p class="cn">不收缺页的练习册</p><ul><li>B: Complete, age-appropriate books are accepted.<br>内容完整、适龄的旧书正是接收范围。</li><li>C: The activity expressly accepts suitable used books.<br>活动明确接收合适旧书，并非拒绝所有读过的书。</li></ul></div></article><article class="question" id="q35"><h3>35. Which plan meets Xiaoqi’s goal and the event’s rules?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 不检查书页，把有缺页的书先送走</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 为了每区都参加，放弃自己最想修好的布袋</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 先洗袋查书，再按书的状况决定是否分享并修袋</div></div><div class="key"><b>Answer: C</b><p>Her plan prepares the bag, checks book eligibility and keeps mending as the main goal.</p><p class="cn">先洗袋、查书既符合规则，也保留修袋主目标；无需自带工具。</p><b>Evidence</b><p class="cn">工具由老师提供</p><p class="cn">先把袋子洗好，再检查书页</p><p class="cn">她最想完成的仍是修好布袋</p><ul><li>A: Missing-page items are expressly excluded.<br>缺页物品被明确排除。</li><li>B: Visiting every area is not required, and abandoning the bag contradicts her priority.<br>不必每区都去，放弃布袋反而违背首要目标。</li></ul></div></article></div></section><h3>R4 · Questions 36–40</h3><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-R4a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 36</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">“少用一次性杯子”活动只针对本周的读书分享会。学校鼓励同学带自己的杯子，但忘带的人可以借用会场清洗好的杯子，结束后放回指定位置。通知提醒，活动不是要求大家马上扔掉家里所有旧杯子，也不限制正常喝水。负责人希望先从一次活动开始，看看怎样做更方便。</p></div><p class="gloss">一次性: single-use</p><p class="gloss">指定: designated</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q36"><h3>36. Which statement correctly describes the initiative’s scope?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 要求全校立刻扔掉所有旧杯子</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 先在本周分享会试行，忘带杯子可以借</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 本周没有自带杯子的人都不能喝水</div></div><div class="key"><b>Answer: B</b><p>The notice limits the trial to this event and supplies a borrowing option.</p><p class="cn">通知限定在本次活动试行，并提供借杯办法。</p><b>Evidence</b><p class="cn">只针对本周的读书分享会</p><p class="cn">忘带的人可以借用会场清洗好的杯子</p><ul><li>A: It explicitly rejects throwing out all old cups.<br>原文明确不是要扔掉所有旧杯子。</li><li>C: It says normal drinking is not restricted and allows borrowed cups.<br>通知说不限制正常喝水，也允许借杯。</li></ul></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-R4b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 37, 38 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">小青的两周记录：以前我总在睡前才找第二天要用的东西，有时一边找一边看手机，早上又要确认一次。这两周我试着吃完晚饭就把书包整理好，睡前留十分钟听轻松的音乐。不是每天都按计划做到，不过我把做到和没做到的日子都记了下来。<br>第二周末，我发现自己早上少找了几次作业本，出门时也没有那么急。我愿意再试两周，看看遇到作业多的时候还能不能坚持。朋友建议我直接说“这个办法人人都该用”，我没有这样写：这些只是我的记录，也可能有别的原因影响那几天的感受。我想先继续观察，再决定怎样调整。</p></div><p class="gloss">确认: check/confirm</p><p class="gloss">观察: observe</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q37"><h3>37. What change does Xiaoqing explicitly report?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 从此每天都绝不会再着急</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 已经证明这个办法适合所有人</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 早上找作业本的次数少了几次</div></div><div class="key"><b>Answer: C</b><p>She reports a limited reduction in searching for a notebook.</p><p class="cn">她报告的是有限次数的减少，并非永久保证。</p><b>Evidence</b><p class="cn">自己早上少找了几次作业本</p><ul><li>A: The record does not make an absolute daily guarantee.<br>记录没有作出每天绝不着急的保证。</li><li>B: She expressly declines to generalize to everyone.<br>她明确没有推广为人人适用。</li></ul></div></article><article class="question" id="q38"><h3>38. Why does she decide to keep observing?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 因为两周里她从来没有一次做到计划</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 因为她已经确定所有变化只由音乐造成</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 已有一些变化，但还要看忙碌时是否可坚持</div></div><div class="key"><b>Answer: C</b><p>She links further observation to a busier context and uncertainty about causes.</p><p class="cn">她把继续观察与忙碌时的坚持及原因的不确定联系起来。</p><b>Evidence</b><p class="cn">遇到作业多的时候还能不能坚持</p><p class="cn">也可能有别的原因影响那几天的感受</p><ul><li>A: She records days when she did follow the plan as well as days when she did not.<br>她记录做到和没做到的日子，不是一次也没做到。</li><li>B: She acknowledges possible other causes rather than fixing on music alone.<br>她承认可能有别的原因，并未认定只因音乐。</li></ul></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-R4c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 39, 40 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">去年参加校园寻路活动时，我一心想让小组最快到达。走错一次后，我一直埋怨自己，差点不想继续。队友没有催我，反而请我画下刚才经过的路口。我们虽然没拿到名次，却一起找到了终点。我后来最常想起的，是大家愿意停下来重新商量的那一刻。<br>最近同学邀请我参加新的小组活动。我每周只有两次放学后的短时间，不可能天天准备。我决定先说明这个限制，问能否负责一小段路线记录。如果大家同意，我就按时完成这部分，再听取反馈。这一次，我把给小组的第一条消息改了三遍，最后写的是自己能完成什么、希望得到什么反馈，而不是先问有没有机会拿第一。</p></div><p class="gloss">埋怨: blame/complain about</p><p class="gloss">反馈: feedback</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q39"><h3>39. Which current adjustment is supported by the past experience and present limits?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 承诺每天都能准备，避免提到时间限制</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 说明可用时间，协商一项能完成的路线记录任务</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 只有保证小组第一名才愿意参加</div></div><div class="key"><b>Answer: B</b><p>The reflection values discussion, and the current plan makes a bounded contribution within available time.</p><p class="cn">过去重视商量，当前又有时间限制，因此协商能完成的小任务符合两方面依据。</p><b>Evidence</b><p class="cn">大家愿意停下来重新商量</p><p class="cn">每周只有两次放学后的短时间</p><p class="cn">问能否负责一小段路线记录</p><ul><li>A: Daily preparation contradicts the explicit availability.<br>天天准备与明确空闲相矛盾。</li><li>C: The narrator no longer treats speed as the only goal.<br>叙述者已不把最快当唯一目标。</li></ul></div></article><article class="question" id="q40"><h3>40. What can reasonably be inferred about the writer’s changed view?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 只要出错，以后就不该参加小组活动</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 只要大家一起参加，就不必完成自己的工作</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 更重视可完成的合作过程，而不只看名次</div></div><div class="key"><b>Answer: C</b><p>Continuing with an adjusted role, while committing to finish it, supports a limited constructive reflection.</p><p class="cn">调整角色后仍参与并承诺完成工作，支持一次错误不决定以后、目标可调整的有限结论。</p><b>Evidence</b><p class="cn">问能否负责一小段路线记录</p><p class="cn">而不是先问有没有机会拿第一</p><ul><li>A: The writer is negotiating a new contribution, which does not support permanent withdrawal.<br>作者在协商新的参与方式，不支持以后不再参加的推断。</li><li>B: The current plan explicitly includes completing the assigned part on time.<br>当前计划明确包括按时完成自己的部分。</li></ul></div></article></div></section><h2 class="section-title" id="writing">Writing · 25 minutes</h2><p>W1 and W2 share 25 minutes. Use paper or your own editor; this review page does not save answers.</p><section class="box" id="W1"><p class="eyebrow">writing · W1</p><h2>Reply to a club disagreement</h2><p>Reply to Lin in Chinese. Answer whether you can join Wednesday’s discussion and whether you prefer interviews or a display. Explain your preference. Address the new restriction with a feasible alternative, and ask one relevant clarification or confirmation. You may invent personal details. About 60-90 Chinese characters is guidance, not a minimum.</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">小禾：我们要介绍学校的旧物再用活动。你周三午休能来讨论吗？你更想采访同学，还是做图片展示？现在老师说放学后不能再进教室，大家原来约好的时间不行了。请你想个办法，也告诉我还有什么需要确认。<br>小林</p></div><ul class="checklist"><li>Answer whether you can join Wednesday lunchtime.</li><li>Choose interviews, a display or another relevant format.</li><li>Give a reason for your preference.</li><li>Offer a feasible way to work without after-school access.</li><li>Ask one relevant clarification or confirmation.</li></ul><div class="key"><h3>Illustrative response — other valid answers are possible</h3><p class="cn">小林，周三午休我能参加。我想做展示，因为大家路过时就能看懂重点。放学后不能进教室，我们可以午休时先拍好图片，晚上各自在家整理。周四午休能一起检查最后的内容吗？</p></div><h3>Alternative example</h3><p class="cn">小林，我周三午休要练合唱，不能到场。我更想采访，因为能听到不同的经历。我们可以先在午休时各自录一小段，晚上再整理。我能周二先发问题，请大家替我问吗？</p><h3>Task-specific review rubric</h3><div class="table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Scoring rubric" tabindex="0"><table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>0</th><th>1</th><th>2</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>任务完成</th><td>已提交内容没有提供与本任务要求相关的可评证据。</td><td>回应部分要求，但遗漏关键观察点或与给定条件冲突。</td><td>完成主要要求：Answer whether you can join Wednesday lunchtime.；Choose interviews, a display or another relevant format.；Give a reason for your preference.；Offer a feasible way to work without after-school access.；Ask one relevant clarification or confirmation.</td></tr><tr><th>可理解性</th><td>主要意思无法恢复。</td><td>部分意思可理解，但数处关系或错误使读者／听者需要猜测。</td><td>主要意思清楚，证据、时间和人物可辨；允许不妨碍理解的错误和口音。</td></tr><tr><th>语言运用</th><td>缺少能表达相关意思的中文词句。</td><td>词句能传达部分信息，但原因、条件或变化关系不清。</td><td>用相互连接的中文句子清楚表达回应、理由和替代，不要求特定句型。</td></tr><tr><th>组织或回应相关性</th><td>缺少相关回应或可辨的内容联系。</td><td>部分相关但顺序、衔接或比较依据不够清楚。</td><td>回应与来信相对应，读者能跟随选择、约束和澄清。</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>A refusal can fully meet the task if explained and accompanied by a feasible alternative.</li><li>Either format is acceptable; no unique opinion or required sentence pattern.</li><li>Check all five observations without mechanically awarding a point for each.</li></ul><p class="badge">Manual /8 · no automatic grade</p></section><section class="box" id="W2"><p class="eyebrow">writing · W2</p><h2>When an activity turned out differently</h2><p>Using the fictional activity card, write connected Chinese paragraphs for a classmate about an experience that changed your view. Include its time and context, at least two actions in sequence, the contrast between expectation and outcome, a reason or feeling, and one reflection or next step. You may add plausible details consistent with the card. About 140-180 Chinese characters is guidance, not a minimum.</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">虚构活动卡<br>时间：上个月一个周六上午<br>地点：学校旧物再用活动<br>原先期待：担心不会修东西，觉得只能旁观<br>经过：先听老师介绍；帮助整理布袋；和同学一起修好松开的提手<br>结果：虽然不快，仍然帮助了别人<br>感受和下一步：自行选择，可表达仍有困难，但须与材料一致</p></div><ul class="checklist"><li>Establish last month’s Saturday morning and the school reuse activity.</li><li>Describe one action from the card.</li><li>Describe a second action in a consistent sequence.</li><li>Contrast the original expectation with what happened.</li><li>Explain a feeling or a reason.</li><li>State a specific reflection or next step.</li></ul><div class="key"><h3>Illustrative response — other valid answers are possible</h3><p class="cn">上个月一个周六上午，我第一次参加学校的旧物再用活动。出发前，我担心自己不会修东西，只能站在旁边看。到了以后，我先听老师介绍，再帮同学整理带来的布袋。后来一个同学的袋子提手松了，我们一起找出问题，跟着老师慢慢修好。虽然我做得不快，大家还是谢谢我帮忙。我原来以为只有技术好的人才能参加，结果发现认真听、愿意合作也很有用。下次我想先学会一种简单的整理方法，再主动负责一小部分工作。</p></div><h3>Task-specific review rubric</h3><div class="table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Scoring rubric" tabindex="0"><table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>0</th><th>1</th><th>2</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>任务完成</th><td>已提交内容没有提供与本任务要求相关的可评证据。</td><td>回应部分要求，但遗漏关键观察点或与给定条件冲突。</td><td>完成主要要求：Establish last month’s Saturday morning and the school reuse activity.；Describe one action from the card.；Describe a second action in a consistent sequence.；Contrast the original expectation with what happened.；Explain a feeling or a reason.；State a specific reflection or next step.</td></tr><tr><th>可理解性</th><td>主要意思无法恢复。</td><td>部分意思可理解，但数处关系或错误使读者／听者需要猜测。</td><td>主要意思清楚，证据、时间和人物可辨；允许不妨碍理解的错误和口音。</td></tr><tr><th>语言运用</th><td>缺少能表达相关意思的中文词句。</td><td>词句能传达部分信息，但原因、条件或变化关系不清。</td><td>用中文连接过去经过、期待与结果以及反思，常见时态标志或连接词足以完成任务。</td></tr><tr><th>组织或回应相关性</th><td>缺少相关回应或可辨的内容联系。</td><td>部分相关但顺序、衔接或比较依据不够清楚。</td><td>经过顺序可辨，期待、结果和反思相互关联，段落或句组清楚。</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>A critical or mixed feeling is valid if supported by the given experience.</li><li>No need to claim mastery of repair or reproduce every card label.</li><li>A reflection must follow from the experience; copying the card alone gives limited organization evidence.</li></ul><p class="badge">Manual /8 · no automatic grade</p></section><h2 class="section-title" id="speaking">Speaking · 10 minutes</h2><section class="box" id="S1"><p class="eyebrow">speaking · S1</p><h2>Discuss a goal and a change of plan</h2><p>Respond in Chinese to four fixed prompts from a classmate about a school project. Each file already contains two plays. Play it once, then allow 15 seconds to prepare and up to 30 seconds to respond. Link your opinion, an experience, an alternative and a next step. You may invent details. All four responses form one task /8; this is not an adaptive conversation.</p><p>You and a classmate are preparing a short introduction for a school activity. Personal experience may be fictional.</p><ul class="checklist"><li>State an opinion or need.</li><li>Use an experience to explain a reason.</li><li>Respond to a new condition with a feasible alternative.</li><li>Explain a final choice and next step.</li></ul><h3>S1-1</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/s1-1.mp3"></audio><p class="cn">我们要介绍学校的一项活动。你希望别人先了解什么？为什么？</p><p class="cn">Example: 我希望别人先知道自己能做什么，因为很多同学和我一样，看到长介绍会不知道从哪里开始。</p><h3>S1-2</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/s1-2.mp3"></audio><p class="cn">说说你以前参加活动的一次经历。它怎样影响了你的想法？</p><p class="cn">Example: 我第一次参加时，只看别人做，没有问问题。后来老师让我试一小步，我才觉得自己也能参与，所以我想先给大家一个小体验。</p><h3>S1-3</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/s1-3.mp3"></audio><p class="cn">现在活动室不能用，我们只有教室门口的一张桌子。可以怎样改？</p><p class="cn">Example: 我们可以把体验缩小，只用几张图片和一个简单材料，不安排需要很多空间的步骤。这样一张桌子也够用。</p><h3>S1-4</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/s1-4.mp3"></audio><p class="cn">最后你建议用什么办法？你先负责哪一部分，还要确认什么？</p><p class="cn">Example: 我建议用图片加简单体验。我先整理三张步骤图，再问老师门口能放桌子的时间。如果那时太挤，就只做展示。</p><p class="note">Each file already plays the prompt twice. Play it once; then prepare for 15 seconds and respond for up to 30 seconds. Four responses are one /8 task.</p><h3>Task-specific review rubric</h3><div class="table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Scoring rubric" tabindex="0"><table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>0</th><th>1</th><th>2</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>任务完成</th><td>已提交内容没有提供与本任务要求相关的可评证据。</td><td>回应部分要求，但遗漏关键观察点或与给定条件冲突。</td><td>完成主要要求：表达相关需要或看法；用经历说明理由；回应新约束并提出替代；解释最后选择及下一步</td></tr><tr><th>可理解性</th><td>主要意思无法恢复。</td><td>部分意思可理解，但数处关系或错误使读者／听者需要猜测。</td><td>主要意思清楚，证据、时间和人物可辨；允许不妨碍理解的错误和口音。</td></tr><tr><th>语言运用</th><td>缺少能表达相关意思的中文词句。</td><td>词句能传达部分信息，但原因、条件或变化关系不清。</td><td>用相互连接的中文说明需要、经历、理由和条件变化；不以词汇复杂度或口音判断。</td></tr><tr><th>组织或回应相关性</th><td>缺少相关回应或可辨的内容联系。</td><td>部分相关但顺序、衔接或比较依据不够清楚。</td><td>四轮相关且彼此大体一致，能解释或修正先前选择；合理拒绝也可。</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Judge all four responses once using the /8 rubric; never multiply the score by four.</li><li>Allow a learner to explain a change of mind rather than requiring identical wording throughout.</li><li>A missing turn is a partial submission; preserve the technical-failure state for failed recording.</li></ul><p class="badge">Manual /8 · no automatic grade</p></section><section class="box" id="S2"><p class="eyebrow">speaking · S2</p><h2>Recommend a school action</h2><p>Recommend one of the two supplied plans to your class. Compare the plans, support your recommendation with two details from the card, identify one limitation, and give a practical next step. Either choice can receive full credit if its constraints are addressed. You have 60 seconds to prepare and up to 120 seconds to speak. Instructions are on screen, not a separate audio prompt.</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">班级情况：20人，周六上午有空，希望多数同学能参与；材料总预算50元。<br>甲：旧书分享，周六9:00–11:00，免费，每人带一本内容完整的书；图书角同时最多10人，可分批；需要2位同学整理推荐单。<br>乙：布袋修补，周六9:30–11:30，老师提供工具和补布，共需材料费30元；同时最多12人，本周只有这一场；学习者须带洗净的布袋。<br>可以推荐任一方案，但要说明怎样处理人数、准备或其他限制。</p></div><ul class="checklist"><li>Compare a relevant feature of both plans.</li><li>Make a clear recommendation.</li><li>Give a first supporting detail from the card.</li><li>Give a different second supporting detail.</li><li>Identify a limitation of the recommended plan.</li><li>Propose a next step that addresses it.</li></ul><div class="key"><h3>Illustrative response — other valid answers are possible</h3><p class="cn">我建议先做甲的旧书分享。两个方案都在周六上午，班里同学可以参加。甲不用花材料费，也适合大家从家里找一本完整的书，准备比较容易。乙可以学到修补方法，而且老师提供工具，也很有意义。不过乙只能接收十二个人，班里有二十个人，不能让所有人同时参加。甲也有一个限制：图书角不大，如果每个人都同时来会太挤。我们可以先统计想参加的人，分两批送书，再请愿意的同学整理推荐单。如果以后有人想修袋，可以另外向老师询问乙活动的下一次时间。</p></div><h3>Alternative example</h3><p class="cn">如果先统计后发现只有十二位同学想修袋，也可以推荐乙。材料费三十元在预算内，老师又提供工具，大家能学会一种继续使用旧物的方法。不过不能直接承诺二十个人都参加这一场。应先报名确认人数，并问没有布袋或这次不能参加的同学是否愿意以后再参加；若大多数人都想同时参加，就改选可以分批的甲。</p><h3>Task-specific review rubric</h3><div class="table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Scoring rubric" tabindex="0"><table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>0</th><th>1</th><th>2</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>任务完成</th><td>已提交内容没有提供与本任务要求相关的可评证据。</td><td>回应部分要求，但遗漏关键观察点或与给定条件冲突。</td><td>完成主要要求：Compare a relevant feature of both plans.；Make a clear recommendation.；Give a first supporting detail from the card.；Give a different second supporting detail.；Identify a limitation of the recommended plan.；Propose a next step that addresses it.</td></tr><tr><th>可理解性</th><td>主要意思无法恢复。</td><td>部分意思可理解，但数处关系或错误使读者／听者需要猜测。</td><td>主要意思清楚，证据、时间和人物可辨；允许不妨碍理解的错误和口音。</td></tr><tr><th>语言运用</th><td>缺少能表达相关意思的中文词句。</td><td>词句能传达部分信息，但原因、条件或变化关系不清。</td><td>用中文明确表达比较、两项依据、限制和建议，允许同义改述。</td></tr><tr><th>组织或回应相关性</th><td>缺少相关回应或可辨的内容联系。</td><td>部分相关但顺序、衔接或比较依据不够清楚。</td><td>先明确选择或比较，再用依据解释，限制与下一步能衔接。</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>A is the simpler route to broad participation; B remains valid if actual interest and one-session capacity are explicitly handled.</li><li>Do not invent a second workshop session for B or assume the capacity can be waived.</li><li>Two distinct supporting details and an acknowledged limitation are the target; no professional environmental knowledge needed.</li></ul><p class="badge">Manual /8 · no automatic grade</p></section></main></body></html>